From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:22:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-75: toolbox Enter adds the selected tool, like WPF
 (0.75.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Part 3 of "改得跟WPF 操作模式一樣" (EastSun 20260930), from Microsoft's "Working
with elements in XAML Designer": "Double-click an element in the Toolbox (or
select an element in the Toolbox and press Enter)". Enter in the toolbox view
used to pick the tool up only (then a click on the surface); now it adds it at
once, like the double-click: the command lets VS Code select the focused item
first (list.select -- the arrow keys move the focus, not the selection), and
the pick-up that selection runs is skipped for that moment. A click still picks
the tool up; a double-click still adds.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 158, smoke 161, panels, real VS Code 147): smoke
(Enter with TLabel selected and Panel2 chosen -> Label9 in Panel2; list.select
ran; the tool not picked up).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
